> Module Estimated_payments
> Using Rounding as R

# Estimated tax payments: Form 1040 line 26

Catala module for Direct File `estimatedPayments.xml` (issue #25, `scope.md`
section 3.7). It computes Form 1040 line 26, "2024 estimated tax payments and
amount applied from 2023 return" (`f1040--2024.pdf` p 2), from the filer's
yes/no answer and the amount, and it reproduces the one knockout that module
defines: payments made under a different legal name.

Conventions: `catala/CONVENTIONS.md`. Inputs are complete (section 3), so the
DF `IsComplete` tests and `estimatedTaxesIsComplete` are not modelled. The
oracle comparison is `make difftest SCOPE=estimated_payments`.

Facts skipped: `/estimatedTaxesIsComplete` (screen-flow state, section 3),
`/paidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouseOptions` (UI option list: the enumeration
below carries all four values, and the MFJ gate on `spouseDid`/`bothDid` is a
UI restriction), `/primaryFilerDivorcedSpouseTaxID` and
`/secondaryFilerDivorcedSpouseTaxID` (identity data printed on the form, not
used in any computation).

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration PaidWithFormerSpouse:
  -- SpouseDid
  -- BothDid
  -- TpDid
  -- Neither

declaration scope EstimatedPayments:
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /paidEstimatedTaxesOrFromLastYear (Writable Boolean)
  input paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year content boolean
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /estimatedTaxPaymentWritable (Writable Dollar)
  input estimated_tax_payment_writable content money
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /paidEstimatedTaxesOrFromLastYearUnderDifferentName
  input paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year_under_different_name content boolean
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /paidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouse (Writable Enum)
  input paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse content PaidWithFormerSpouse

  # Form 1040 line 26. DF: estimatedPayments.xml /estimatedAndFromLastYear
  output estimated_and_from_last_year content money

  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /spousePaidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouse
  output spouse_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse condition
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /tpPaidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouse
  output tp_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse condition
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /someTPPaidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouse
  output some_tp_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse condition

  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /knockoutPaidEstimatedTaxesUnderDifferentLastName
  output ko_knockout_paid_estimated_taxes_under_different_last_name condition
  output unsupported condition
```

## Form 1040 line 26

The 1040 instructions for line 26 (`i1040gi--2024.pdf`, PDF p 37): "Enter
any estimated federal income tax payments you made for 2024. Include any
overpayment that you applied to your 2024 estimated tax from your 2023 return
or an amended return (Form 1040-X)."

Direct File asks for the amount only when the filer says they paid, and
rounds the result to whole dollars (`Round` around the `Switch`). With
complete inputs the "if complete and true" test is the flag itself.

```catala
scope EstimatedPayments:
  # Form 1040 line 26, f1040--2024.pdf p 2
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /estimatedAndFromLastYear
  definition estimated_and_from_last_year equals
    R.round_dollar of (
      if paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year
      then estimated_tax_payment_writable
      else $0
    )
```

## Payments made with a former spouse

The instructions (`i1040gi--2024.pdf`, PDF p 37): "Divorced taxpayers. If you got
divorced in 2024 and you made joint estimated tax payments with your former
spouse, enter your former spouse's SSN in the space provided on the front of
Form 1040 or 1040-SR." These facts only decide which former-spouse SSN fields
the form shows; they do not change line 26 and Direct File defines no
knockout for them (`flow.xml` lists only the different-name knockout). They
are outputs so the caller can see them.

```catala
scope EstimatedPayments:
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /spousePaidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouse
  definition spouse_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse equals
    paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse = BothDid
    or paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse = SpouseDid

  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /tpPaidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouse
  definition tp_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse equals
    paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse = BothDid
    or paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse = TpDid

  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /someTPPaidEstimatedTaxesWithFormerSpouse
  definition some_tp_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse equals
    spouse_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse
    or tp_paid_estimated_taxes_with_former_spouse
```

## Name change knockout

The instructions (`i1040gi--2024.pdf`, PDF p 37): "Name change. If you changed your
name and you made estimated tax payments using your former name, attach a
statement to the front of Form 1040 or 1040-SR that explains all the payments
you and your spouse made in 2024 and the name(s) and SSN(s) under which you
made them." Direct File cannot attach a statement, so it knocks the flow out.

```catala
scope EstimatedPayments:
  # DF: estimatedPayments.xml /knockoutPaidEstimatedTaxesUnderDifferentLastName
  # (flow.xml line 65, aggregated into /flowIsKnockedOut)
  rule ko_knockout_paid_estimated_taxes_under_different_last_name
    under condition
      paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year
      and paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year_under_different_name
    consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported
    under condition ko_knockout_paid_estimated_taxes_under_different_last_name
    consequence fulfilled
```
